1 NAME Peder Olson /Fjelde/ Øvre Fjelde
2 GIVN Peder Olson
2 SURN Fjelde
2 NSFX Øvre Fjelde
2 _MARNM Øvre Fjelde
1 NAME Peder Olsen Øvre Fjelde
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 FEB 1825
2 PLAC Øvre Fjelde
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jørpeland
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 OCT 1910
2 ADDR
3 CITY Manly
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/56684880/peder_olsen_fjelde
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Olsen Fjelde was born February 13, 1825 at Ovre Fjelde farm, Roga​​land, Norway to Ole Endresen Ovre Fjelde (1778-1860) and Berte Olsdatter Hogstad (1789-1865).
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder was baptized February 20, 1825 and confirmed October 17, 1841 both at Strand, Rogaland, Norway.
2 CONT Birth/baptismal record at Norwegian Digital Archives on-line for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway, 1816-1833, page 44, entry # 4: Peder Olsen Ovre Fjeldes.
2 CONT Confirmation record at Norw. Dig. Archives for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway 1834-1854, page 278, entry #5.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder married​ ​Martha Larsdatter Forland March 23, 18​52​ at Strand, Rogaland, Norway. Marriage record at Norwegian Digital Archives for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway 1834-1854, page 326, entry # 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had 11 children:
2 CONT Inger Pedersdatter (November 23, 1852 Norway to May 3, 1899 Grafton, Walsh, ND; FAG Memorial# 29849792);
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Pedersen (January 1, 1855 Norway to August 23, 1941 Cedar, Mitchell, IA; FAG Memorial #56660804);
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthe (born April 4, 1857 Norway, married Oswald Strand, then Ed Rolla, died November 8, 1938 Worth, Iowa);
2 CONT
2 CONT Edvard Jorgen Laurits (born December 6, 1859 Norway, died July 1, 1934 Edinburg, Walsh, North Dakota);
2 CONT
2 CONT Endre (Andrew) (September 9, 1862 Norway to April 20, 1934 USA); FAG Memorial# 56652055.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars (born February 5, 1865, died April 21, 1865 both at Strand, Rogaland, Norway);
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars (Lewis) (born April 17, 1866 Norway, died July 3, 1946 Manly, Worth, Iowa);
2 CONT
2 CONT Marte (born December 1, 1868 Norway, died November 15, 1941 America);
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder (born March 10, 1872 Norway, died September 24, 1872 Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa);
2 CONT
2 CONT Petra Emilie (born November 1873 Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa, married Andrew Fods 1896, died December 21, 1961);
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder (born September 1, 1876 Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa, died September 24, 1949 Ann Arbor, Michigan).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family emigrated to Mitchell County, Iowa in 1872 with 7 children leaving Norway April 5, 1872 and arriving at Quebec, Canada May 21, 1872 on the ship Brodrene.
2 CONT Ship's list: Peder Olsen Fjelde age 46, Martha Larsdatter age 38, Ole 17, Inger 19, Bertha 15, Edvard 12, Endre 9, Lars 6, Martha 3, Peder 1 month. (Emigration arrival record ship's list can be found on Ancestry.com).
2 CONT Emigration record leaving at Norwegian Digital Archives on line for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway 1855-1881, page 350 (right side of pages), entries # 3 through 12: Peder O Fjelde, Marthe Larsdatter, Inger, Ole, Berte, Edvard
2 CONC  Torgrim Lauritz, Endre, Lars, Marte, Peder.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family traveled on by train and finally arrived at Mitchell County, Iowa where they lived with relatives about a year before buying farmland. They were early members of the Rock Creek Lutheran Church at Meroa, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family found in the 1880 to 1905 censuses at Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa:
2 CONT 1880: Peter Field 57, Martha Field 50, Ole Field 25, Edward Field 19, Andrew Field 17, Lars Field 15, Martha Field 10, Emalia Field 6, Peter Field 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1885: Peter O Tjelde 60, Martha Tjelde 57, Edward Tjelde 24, Andrew Tjelde 22, Louis Tjelde 18, Martha Tjelde 16, Amelia Tjelde 11, Peter Tjelde 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900: Peder Fjelde 75, Martha Fjelde 69, Peder Fjelde 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Olsen Fjelde die​d October 31, 1910 at Manly, Worth, Iowa and was buried at the Rock Creek Lutheran Church Cemetery, Meroa, Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial #56684880.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Censuses transcribed as found without fixing spelling errors.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Credit: Deidre Badker
