1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/29849792/inger_birk
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger Pedersdatter (Ovre) Fjelde was born November 23, 1852 at Ovre Fjelde farm, Strand, Rogaland, Norway to Peder Olsen Fjelde and Martha Larsdatter, the oldest of their eleven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger was baptized December 25, 1852 at Strand and confirmed also at Strand on June 10, 1867.
2 CONT Birth/baptismal record at Norwegian Digital Archives on-line for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway, 1834-1854, page 109, entry # 30, lists sponsors.
2 CONT Confirmation record at Nor. Dig. Arch. online for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway 1855-1881, page 195, entry # 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger emigrated in the spring of 1872 with her parents and siblings to America.
2 CONT Emigration record leaving at Norwegian Digital Archives on line for Strand in Strand, Rogaland, Norway 1855-1881, page 350 (right side of pages), entries # 3 through 12: Peder O Fjelde, Marthe Larsdatter, Inger, Ole, Berte, Edvard
2 CONC  Torgrim Lauritz, Endre, Lars, Marte, Peder (born March 10, 1872).
2 CONT Emigrated to America, arriving at Quebec, Canada May 21, 1872 on the ship Brodrene. (Emigration record can be found on Ancestry.com): Peder Olsen Fjelde age 46, Martha Larsdatter age 38, son Ole 17, daughter Inger 19, daughter Ber
2 CONC tha 15, son Edvard 12, son Endre 9, son Lars 6, daughter Martha 3, son Peder 1 month.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Ingebrit Birk (Birkedal) on July 22, 1873. Ingebrit born 1851, died 1933, he is also buried at South Trinity Cemetery).
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had 9 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger died May 3, 1899 at rural Grafton, Walsh, North Dakota and was buried at the South Trinity Cemetery, Grafton, N.D.
