1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Anna L. (Hopkins) Kugel''', a former Peabody resident, died Monday in her home. She was 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Malden, she was educated in the Malden public schools. Before she retired, Mrs. Kugel was employed at Eaton Pharmacy in Salem and Tilton Pharmacy in Beverly.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had lived in Salem for six years, and before that had lived in Peabody for 35 years. She was the wife of the late Rolf Kugel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Kugel leaves four sons, Keith of Rhode Island, Christopher of Ipswich, Scott of Salem, and Erik of Walpole; five daughters, Kristein Page of Virginia, Robin Kugel of Florida, Heidi Marvill of Easton, and Dawn Kugel and Liza D
2 CONC avis, both of Beverly; a sister, Marilyn Lawson of Florida; 32 grandchildren; and two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT A private service will be held at a later date.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna L. (Hopkins) Kugel''', 70, of Salem and formerly of Peabody, died Monday evening at her home, surrounded by her family, following a brief illness. She was the devoted wife of the late Rolf Kugel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Malden, she was the daughter of the late Kenneth and Alice (Mortonson) Hopkins. She was raised and educated in Malden and attended Malden Public Schools. She later lived in Peabody for over 35 years, spent three years livi
2 CONC ng in New Hampshire and for the past 6 years, lived in Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT She worked for Eaton Pharmacy in Salem and later for Tilton Pharmacy in Beverly before retiring a few years ago. Anna enjoyed playing bingo, going to yard sales, and more importantly, she enjoyed spending time with her children an
2 CONC d grand children.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by 4 sons and daughters-in-law, Keith and Jean Kugel of RI, Christopher and Lynn Kugel of Ipswich, Scott and Angela Kugel of Salem, Erik and Ellen Kugel of Walpole, five daughters and three sons-in-law, Kristein an
2 CONC d Donald Page of VA, Robin Kugel of FL., Liza and Rich Davis of Beverly, Heidi and Don Marvill of Easton, and Dawn Kugel of Beverly, a sister, Marilyn Lawson of FL, and is also survived by 32 grandchildren, 2 great grandchildren, 
2 CONC and many nieces, nephews, and cousins. She was the mother of the late Christian Kugel and her late dog, Major.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following cremation, a private family memorial service will be held at a later date. Expressions of sympathy can be made in her name to the North East Animal Shelter, 204 Highland Ave, Salem, MA 01970.
