2 CONT
2 CONT  Palmer M Levin, 96
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Forks Herald (ND) - Thursday, March 1, 1990.
2 CONT
2 CONT Palmer M. Levin, 96, Minot, formerly of Edinburg, died Tuesday, Feb. 27, 1990, in Trinity Nursing Care Facility, Minot.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 11 a.m. Saturday in Trinity Lutheran Church, Edinburg. Visitation will be from 4 to 7 p.m. Friday in Tollefson Funeral Home, Edinburg, and an hour before services in the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Palmer M. Levin was born Sept. 6, 1893, near Edinburg, the son of Aaron and Martha Levin. He attended a country school near there and later what is now North Dakota State University. He married Lena Ulberg Jan. 30, 1918, and they 
2 CONC lived on the family farm near Park River, N.D. He served in the North Dakota Legislature from 1935 to 1953. He was on the first legislative committee and, in 1949, was elected speaker of the House. He was appointed in 1950 to the 
2 CONC State Civil Defense Council and in 1953, was given a federal appointment to serve on the State Agricultural Stabilization and Conservation Committee, serving as its chairman from 1954 to 1957. He was appointed to the State Board o
2 CONC f Administration in 1957. They lived in Minot since 1968, and she died Dec. 4, 1974.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors are his son, Curtis, Tigard, Ore.; daughters, Marvel (Mrs. Alford) Setness, Grand Forks, Rhoda (Mrs. Ben) Bramble, Auburn, Calif., Mavis (Mrs. Kirk) Bale, Minot; 10 grandchildren; six great-grandchildren; sister, Alice S
2 CONC ussex, Moorhead; and several nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by an infant son.
2 CONT
2 CONT CITE THIS RECORD Grand Forks Herald (North Dakota) 01 March 1990, obit for PALMER LEVIN, GenealogyBank.com (https://www.genealogybank.com/doc/obituaries/obit/0FE5FAC5C1AAC6D0-0FE5FAC5C1AAC6D0 : accessed 21 August 2019)
2 CONT --------------------
