1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/56658017/inger_fjelde
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger Olson was born March 19, 1848 at Malmo, Sweden to Ole Peterson and Karen Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT She emigrated 1878 to Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger married Ole Pedersen Fjelde (later spelled Field) (b January 1, 1855 Strand, Rogaland, Norway, d August 23, 1941 Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa) on November 10, 1880 at the First Lutheran Church at St Ansgar, Mitchell, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had 4 children who were all born at Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa: Oscar Olesen (b February 9, 1882, d April 11, 1953 Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa);
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter (b December 7, 1883, d November 6, 1969 Mason City, Cerro Gordo, Iowa);
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin P (b August 31, 1885, d October 12, 1952 Mason City, Iowa) and
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl (b August 13, 1887, d January 19, 1979 Osage, Mitchell, Iowa).
2 CONT
2 CONT Found in the 1885 - 1930 censuses living on a farm at Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa:
2 CONT 1885: Oley P Tjelde 32, Inger Tjelde 23, Oscar Tjelde 3, Peter Tjelde 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900: Ole P Fjelde 45, Inger Fjelde 52, Oscar Fjelde 18, Peder Fjelde 16, Martin Fjelde 14, Karl Fjelde 12.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910: Ole Peder Fjelde 53[55], Inga Fjelde 52, Peter Fjelde 26, Martin Fjelde 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920: Martin Field 34, Emily K Field 34, Peter Field 36, Oleo P Fjelde 65, Inger Fjelde 71.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1925: Ole P Fjield (Field) 70, Jordar Fjield (Inger Field) 76.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930: Ole P Field 75, Inger Field 82.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason City Globe Gazette, November 27, 1930:
2 CONT Mr and Mrs Field Celebrate Wedding Anniversary: Mr and Mrs Ole Pedersen Field celebrated their golden wedding anniversary when they were guests at a dinner at the home of their son and daughter in law, Mr & Mrs Oscar Field, north 
2 CONC of Nora Springs. Yellow chrysanthemums, golden bells and baskets of roses were used throughout the rooms. The wedding cake was a gift of their granddaughter, Mrs Alvin Christiansen.
2 CONT The Rev and Mrs S M Stenby of Clear Lake were present and the Rev gave a brief talk and presented a number of gifts to the couple. Mr and Mrs Lewis Field and Mrs Bertha Rolla of Manly were among the guests.
2 CONT Mr & Mrs Field were married in 1880 in St Ansgar by the Rev. John Olson. They have four sons who were present at the affair. The remainder of the time was spent informally.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inger Field died October 4, 1938 at Cedar, Mitchell, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Credit: Deidre Badker
