2 CONT
2 CONT Car Crash Is Fatal To Martin Field
2 CONT
2 CONT Manslaughter Charge Is Filed Against Nibbe of Amboy, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT An auto crash which occured about 6:45 a.m. Sunday, Oct. 12, on Highway 9, two miles east of Manly, proved fatal to Martin O. Field, 67, of Nora Springs, prominent farmer in the Rock Creek community north of here. Mr. Field died a
2 CONC t 10:40 a.m. Sunday in a Mason City hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Nibbe, 38, of Amboy, Minn., was charged with man slaughter Monday as a result of the accident. Sheriff A. J. Conner of Northwood, who investigated the crash, said there were indications that Nibbe's car was over the center
2 CONC  line of the highway when the two cars collided headon. The officer said there were indications that Nibbe had been drinking and a blood test was made.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. and Mrs. Field were going west, having been on their way to a church convention at Jackson, Minn. Nibbe's car was going east, the left fronts of both vehicles colliding.
2 CONT
2 CONT Field's forehead was severely lacerated. Reports from the hospital stated that he suffered a concussion. His wife was also taken to the hospital with a fractured left leg, cuts and bruises. She was reported in fair condition early
2 CONC  this week.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nibbe was also hospitalized with cuts and bruises. He was released from the hospital Monday, at which time the manslaughter charge was filed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Field is survived by his wife, the former Emily Bistol; one son, Irving Field of Nora Springs; a daughter, Margaret Ann, who is an instructor in the Forest City school; two grandchildren; and three brothers, Peter, Carl and Os
2 CONC car Field.
2 CONT (1952)
